<title>USA: U.S. Sept business inventories rose 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sept business inventories rose 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. September business inventories rose 0.1 percent after a revised 0.3 percent increase in August. It said September business sales rose 0.8 percent after a revised 0.2 percent decrease in August.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES: September   August--Rev from     July</p>
<p>Total Business  1,006.21  1,005.44  1,007.03  1,002.40  Durable Goods     608.29    605.87    605.68    601.98</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  397.91    399.57    401.35    400.42</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES: September  August--Rev from	July</p>
<p> Manufacturers     437.13   435.69    435.61     434.45</p>
<p> Retailers	   313.55   310.93    311.11     308.86</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     89.49    88.22     87.83</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 255.52   258.82    260.31     259.10</p>
<p>    SALES:	 September  August--Rev from	July</p>
<p> Total Business    723.45   717.53    717.09     719.18</p>
<p> Durable Goods     359.04   353.81    353.69     354.62</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  364.41   363.72    363.41     364.56</p>
<p>    SALES:	 September  August--Rev from	July</p>
<p> Manufacturers     315.28   312.85    312.64     312.40</p>
<p> Retailers	   206.20   204.60    204.25     204.72</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     50.89    50.02     49.98</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 201.97   200.09    200.20     202.06</p>
<p> Inventory-To-   September  August--Rev from	July</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.39     1.40	1.40	 1.39</p>
<p>The inventory-to-sales ratio is a measure of how long it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
<p>The September ratio was the lowest since the department began the series in 1982, matching readings in July and May 1996, a department spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected September business inventories to rise 0.2 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised August business inventories from a previously reported 0.5 percent rise, and August sales from a previously reported 0.3 percent decrease.</p>
